n) -- the template has now been proven, independently, across 6 uses spanning forestry, manufacturing, finance, education, real-estate, and repair-services domains, with zero forced fits and one honest, evidence-backed drop.", :event/not-done "Did not attempt iso3166-jor further -- correctly out of scope once confirmed blueprint-only; no code exists there to drive a build-time demo from (this is the SAME class of gap as isic-5820's, ledger seq 3, and isic-2011, both previously identified as out-of-template-scope). Did not investigate how many OTHER repos in the 286/290 cluster-size figures might be similarly affected by shared-checkout staleness (a real, newly-surfaced limitation of any local-disk-based census in this fleet) -- flagged, not fixed, this iteration. Did not force-sync the shared orgs/ checkouts for the 4 newly-fixed repos (unlike ledger seq 6) -- this iteration treated 'never touch shared checkouts, even read-only mutating ones like west update' as the binding instruction; the resulting checkout-lag is expected, understood, and self-explaining via the scanner's own lag field, not a defect. Did not touch checklist items 1/3/5/6/7 for any of the 4 closed repos, nor promote any of them to the flagship cohort table (cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn) -- explicitly out of scope for this iteration's brief (items 2+4 only). Did not update cloud-itonami-flagship-generator-template.edn's own 'Applied this iteration' section -- this ledger entry is the record of the extended track record; the template doc itself needed no adaptation-point changes (all 4 repos used the same :subject subject-key variant already documented, no new ADAPT-point variant was discovered). Did not attempt a 6th repo to backfill iso3166-jor's drop -- per this iteration's explicit guardrail ('drop that repo from the batch... don't let one hard repo block landing the others'), landing 4/5 cleanly was treated as a complete, honest batch result rather than chasing a round number.", :event/s