d via gh api repos/kotoba-lang/industry/merges (commit 16f44577ea1004d167b08bcc4bfb6a05e08cdf28). Advanced manifest/west.yml's industry pin (f6cd5622 -> 16f44577) via the mandated single-entry sha-guarded GitHub API PUT (commit d33eef77a861f74d7995a4943aabc6f5a50cc1c8 on com-junkawasaki/root main), first verifying pure forward progress via gh api compare (ahead_by 2, behind_by 0, merge_base==old pin). IMPORTANT PROCESS FINDING, recorded for future iterations: this iteration's first west.yml PUT attempt used bare /tmp/ filenames (e.g. /tmp/west.yml, /tmp/put-body.json) in violation of this environment's own scratchpad-directory instruction, and got corrupted mid-flight by what appears to be a concurrent session writing to the same shared /tmp paths -- the resulting candidate west.yml silently contained a stale (2026-07-14) revision for an unrelated entry (cloud-itonami-isic-0230) that neither matched local disk nor live GitHub state, and the PreToolUse pin-verify-guard hook correctly caught it as a pin regression across 8+ entries and denied the PUT before it reached GitHub. Root-caused by decoding the actual submitted PUT body myself (not assuming the hook was wrong) and finding the corruption; redid the entire fetch-edit-verify-PUT cycle inside the dedicated scratchpad directory instead (self-verifying the decoded PUT body's content before submitting), which succeeded cleanly on retry -- the guard worked exactly as designed and prevented a real accidental pin regression from landing on main. Synced the shared superproject root (fast-forward, no tracked-file conflicts) and ran `west update --fetch smart industry`, confirmed local HEAD == 16f44577 exactly. Re-ran the fleet-wide scanner (unmodified) over all 1,109 real local checkouts: item6-has-demo-field 407 -> 18 (exact match to item2-likely-generated=18 at that point), all other aggregate fields unchanged (confirming the fix touched only registry.edn / item6, nothing else). Wrote the refreshed scan (975,265 bytes)