o confirmed nonexistent for the sampled subset), not a blind extrapolation of iteration 9's unrelated 12-repo sample to a different population. Did not investigate WHY the pre-Wave5 bulk-default commit (2d7b46db9) set :demo so broadly in the first place, nor whether it should be reverted/disabled to prevent recurrence for future new registry entries -- flagged as a real, separate follow-up: if new numeric-ISIC entries keep getting an auto-default :demo field pointing at their bare Pages root regardless of whether a real demo exists, this same class of drift will recur every time a new repo is registered without also getting a real generator. Did not touch item6 for the 3 new Part-2 closures (isic-563/861/0112) -- consistent with iteration 9's precedent (isic-5520/6910), left as an open, small, well-scoped follow-up (3 registry entries needing either a new :demo field added, in isic-563/0112's case where none exists yet, or verification if one already exists from the bulk-default pass). Did not re-verify the 51 business-id/:repo mismatch entries in registry.edn (upstream data-quality bug, worked around via dual-key correlation same as iteration 5, not fixed at the source). Did not attempt the pre-existing isic-851/isic-6310 cron-slot collision (seq 8, still open), the 35-repo checkout-lag-unknown/orphan west.yml gap (seq 5/7/8, still open), the isic-6310 blocked-by-dirty-.gitignore checkout-lag (seq 8, still open, checkout/lag?=1 unchanged this iteration), or checklist items 1/3/5/7 for any repo -- all explicitly out of scope for this iteration. Did not promote any of the 3 newly-closed repos to the flagship cohort table.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/seq 10, :event/at "2026-07-18T19:21:40Z"}
{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 11, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1391, cloud-itonami-isic-5210, cloud-itonami-isic-6512, cloud-itonami-isic-8010, cloud-itonami-isic-9311, cloud-itonami-isic-9603 (6 closed item2+4+6) + cloud-itonami-isic-0710 (dropped, pre-dispatch) + kotoba-lang/industry (item6 backfill for isic-563/861/0112 + item6 for the 6 new closures)", :event/checklist-stage 2, :event/stage-name "6-way-parallel-template-batch-plus-item6-closed-in-same-pass-plus-item6-debt-backfill", :event/action "First iteration to close items 2+4+6 TOGETHER per repo in a single pass, per this iteration's explicit brief (iterations 6-8 closed 2+4 only and left item6 as accumulating debt that iterations 9/10 then had to spend whole iterations cleaning up). Before dispatching new work, backfilled the item6 gap iteration 10 explicitly left open: isic-563/861/0112 (iteration 10's own Part2 closures) had items 2+4 closed on GitHub but no :demo field in kotoba-lang/industry's registry.edn. Live-curled all 3 samples/operator-console.html URLs FRESH (not trusting local disk or prior ledger claims) -- all 3 returned HTTP 200 with real, distinct, sector-specific <title> tags -- before writing anything. For the new batch: pre-screened 6 shape-matched candidates via LIVE GitHub API tree/grep inspection (git/trees/main?recursive=1 + contents API on operation.cljc), never the local orgs/ checkout, spanning deliberately unrelated, non-adjacent ISIC sectors and never-before-touched real-world domains: isic-1391 (manufacture of knitted/crocheted fabrics, knittingops -- textiles), isic-5210 (warehousing and storage / petroleum tank terminal, terminal -- logistics), isic-6512 (non-life/casualty insurance underwriting, casualty -- finance), isic-9603 (funeral and related activities, funeral -- death care), isic-8010 (private security activities, guardops -- security), isic-9311 (operation of sports facilities, facility -- recreation). A 7th candidate, isic-0710 (min