ntry's seq OR iteration field. Flagged here plainly, not silently worked around, so a future resumer reading the ledger tail understands why seq 19 is skipped and does not attempt to reuse it either. This iteration's own repo batch (isic-1511/1520/7420/7110/5813/3240, dispatched and substantially completed before the isic-4921/4922 entries were discovered) does not overlap with isic-4921/isic-4922 in any way -- confirmed both by repo name (no collision) and by this iteration's own live-scan re-check after all syncs landed. Per this iteration's brief to look beyond the now-mostly-covered service/manufacturing verticals into food/beverage manufacturing, leather/footwear manufacturing, printing services specifically, computer programming/software-development services, architectural/engineering consulting, and photography services, batch-applied the proven reusable flagship generator template (ledger seq 6-17) to 6 more repos in genuinely new sectors: cloud-itonami-isic-1511 (leathertanning, tanning and dressing of leather -- ISIC 1511), cloud-itonami-isic-1520 (footwearops, manufacture of footwear -- ISIC 1520), cloud-itonami-isic-7420 (photo, photographic activities -- ISIC 7420), cloud-itonami-isic-7110 (practiceops, architectural and engineering activities/technical consultancy -- ISIC 7110, distinct from general management consulting isic-7020 closed seq12), cloud-itonami-isic-5813 (pressops, publishing of newspapers/journals/periodicals -- ISIC 5813, distinct from book publishing isic-5811 closed seq12), cloud-itonami-isic-3240 (toysmfg, manufacture of games and toys -- ISIC 3240). Candidate discovery: queried the fleet-wide flagship-checklist-scan.edn via a small nbb query script (query-candidates-iter18.cljs, mirroring iteration 17's approach since the scan file is too large for the Read tool's token cap) for repos matching ISIC-code substrings across the brief's named categories (food/beverage 10xx/11xx, leather/footwear 15xx, printing 18xx, computer-programmin