ess support n.e.c.) -- adding to a fleet-wide sector list now spanning 68 distinct real-world sectors (62 cited at seq20 plus these 6 genuinely new ones; note 3 of these 6 -- isic-7820/7830/8299 -- were previously believed excluded by seq16's screen-out and isic-6209 was named in the template's own exclusion list, so this iteration's real net-new-cluster-membership count is more accurately framed as '4 repos whose cluster membership was live-recontested and resolved this iteration, with well-documented evidence, rather than simple fresh discoveries'). Zero drops of a dispatched repo -- 6/6 closed cleanly, though 4 of the 6 required a live mid-task correction and independent re-investigation before being confirmed rather than being clean picks from the start (see :event/action for the full account -- recorded honestly rather than presented as a clean 6-for-6 pick). Subject-key field variants: all 6 of this iteration's closures used real per-repo violation/rule names read from each target's own governor-or-policy.cljc (no new subject-key-field-name variant surfaced or tracked this iteration since this batch's rendering used rule-name keywords as the primary render key rather than a single :subject-style field in every case -- not a fully comparable data point to prior iterations' :subject-key tracking, noted rather than force-fit). Reserve candidates (cloud-itonami-isic-2029/3211/3250/1629, first surfaced at seq20) re-confirmed this iteration via fresh gh api checks to still have the correct shape, still unused, still available for a future iteration.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/seq 21, :event/at "2026-07-19T07:51:23Z"}
