ross-checked against an actually-observed store-state mutation from the sim run (not just static reading). No isic-4322-class bug found in this batch -- extends the clean streak from every prior iteration back through seq16 (this rollout has never found a second instance of that bug class since seq16 first discovered and fixed it in isic-4322 itself). Two benign-but-notable issues surfaced and were independently confirmed NOT to have caused harm: (1) isic-6612's agent's workflow-dispatch retry loop misfired 5 extra times (6 runs total in a 35-second window) -- verified via `gh api .../actions/runs` that all 6 completed success and the commit history shows only the 2 real commits (work + merge), no duplicate console commits, confirming the workflow's own git-diff guard prevented any actual duplicate write; (2) isic-8030's agent found a genuine (pre-existing, not introduced) design wrinkle in investigation.sim -- its own demo scenario schedules the same investigator twice so 2 of its holds trip BOTH :clearance-tier-gate and :capacity-gate simultaneously instead of isolating one reason each -- the agent correctly did NOT reuse that scenario verbatim and instead built its own request set in render_html.clj that isolates each of 4 hard-hold reasons cleanly, confirmed present in the live-rendered ledger table. Also surfaced (unrelated, correctly left out of scope): isic-6622's test run hit a pre-existing compile error in cloud-itonami-isic-8291's CURRENT origin/main (dossier/llm.cljc:254, a forward-reference bug, confirmed via GitHub API to be the actual live tip, not a stale/shallow-clone artifact) -- blocks intermediation.corporate-intel-test specifically; reported honestly, not papered over, not fixed (out of scope for an isic-6622 item2+4 task; flagged here as a candidate for a future iteration on isic-8291 itself). Local `orgs/` checkouts for all 6 repos re-synced to the exact merged SHAs before computing west.yml pins (3 were stale after their agents worked in isola