dac8502d525..., isic-5224 d38dc7f838f88d09..., isic-7721 d15977723e2b615b...). isic-4322-class commit-node bug check: independently re-read (not just trusted the agent's claim) the actual `:commit` node source of all 6 repos' `operation.cljc` via fresh `gh api contents` fetches -- ALL 6 confirmed CLEAN, each calling real `(store/commit-record! store record)` + `(store/append-ledger! store f)`, never a no-op. Continues the clean streak unbroken since seq16 first discovered and fixed that bug class in isic-4322 itself -- no second instance found in any iteration since, including this one. Grepped each live page for its claimed HARD-hold rule keywords and confirmed all present (isic-6810: no-spec-basis/sanctions-hit/incomplete-documents; isic-8121: site-unverified/effect-not-propose/scope-excluded; isic-7710: account-unverified/effect-not-propose/scope-excluded; isic-6420: no-spec-basis/distribution-exceeds-distributable-reserves/beneficial-ownership-verification-unresolved; isic-5224: shipment-unverified/facility-unregistered; isic-7721: asset-unverified/effect-not-propose/scope-excluded). ITEM 6: re-fetched registry.edn fresh immediately before editing (sha 91f43ba57ac03902625d525309fc554abdaecf1a, unchanged from an earlier capture at the start of this iteration -- no drift in that window), located all 6 entries (3 by :business-id match, 3 only by :repo URL match due to the registry's known business-id!=repo-basename data-quality issue), confirmed zero pre-existing :demo fields, patched via Python text-substitution anchored on each entry's unique `{:id \"<code>\" :name \"` prefix (verified count()==1 per anchor before replacing), re-parsed the FULL patched file with a real EDN reader (cljs.reader, nbb) afterward and asserted industries count unchanged (650==650) and demo-field count moved 86->92 (exactly +6, no others touched). Pushed via sha-guarded gh api PUT (commit f06ea8ac96100652e5def94a816e77e97e5e24f9), re-fetched the merged copy and diffed byte-for-byte against the locally-verified file -- identical. WEST.YML PIN ADVANCE: verified all 6 target repos were ALREADY west-registered (an earlier `grep` against a wrongly-quoted pattern falsely suggested they were orphans; corrected by grepping the actual `name: <repo>` line format before concluding anything -- all 6 had real existing entries, no repos.edn/west-orphan registration needed this iteration, unlike several recent iterations). Verified all 6 pin advances were pure forward progress via `gh api .../compare` BEFORE writing (all showed status=ahead, behind_by=0, merge_base_commit==old pin, ahead_by 4 each) per ADR-2607022900's binding criteria. Patched via the same anchored-line-substitution method (not marker-based hand-editing), verified exactly 6 lines changed via diff before pushing. First PUT attempt hit a genuine 409 (`is at b6de4eeb... but expected 82f50fc3...`) -- a real concurrent write landed on manifest/west.yml between my fetch and my PUT, not a bug in my own logic; re-fetched (blob sha unchanged at the new main tip, confirming the concurrent commit hadn't touched west.yml itself) and retried, which succeeded (commit c3b9b06165c1a374daa46a3c6facaa6ee3319afb). Re-fetched the merged west.yml and diffed byte-for-byte against the locally-verified patched file -- identical, confirming the retry did not clobber any other concurrent pin movement. Synced the superproject's own main checkout to origin THREE times across this iteration (after the initial read, after the west.yml PUT, and once more before writing this entry), hitting the documented shallow-graft `(forced update)`/`unrelated histories` false-positive pattern EVERY time -- confirmed via `gh api .../compare` each time that the true state was a pure fast-forward (status ahead, behind_by=0, merge_base==old local tip) before repairing via `git fetch --deepen` + `git merge --ff-only`, never trusting the local error message alone, exactly per CLAUDE.md's documented procedure. Also synced the local `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry` checkout (remote is named `kotoba-lang` not `origin` in this shared checkout, as seq21 also noted) and all 6 target repos' local `orgs/cloud-itonami/*` checkouts to their new pinned commits -- found and safely `git stash push --` (not dropped) another concurrent session's uncommitted modified file (`docs/adr/0002-netherlands-owner-sale-profile.md`) in the shared isic-6810 checkout before syncing it, per CLAUDE.md's explicit standing instruction; the other 5 checkouts were clean and were synced via a direct fetch+checkout of the exact pinned SHA (detached HEAD, matching west's own normal pin-checkout model) after `--deepen` alone proved insufficient to bridge their shallow-graft boundaries. Re-ran the fleet-wide scanner AFTER all syncs landed: item4-has-regenerate-yml 86->92 (+6), item2-likely-generated 87->93 (+6), item6-has-demo-field 86->92 (+6) -- all three aggregate counters moved by exactly this iteration's 6 closures with no unattributed drift this time (a cleaner attribution than several recent iterations that had +1 unexplained residue from other sessions landing mid-window). Computed the precise item2+4+6-ALL-closed intersection directly (not just the 3 separate aggregates): 85 at this iteration's own first fresh scan, 91 at the final rescan -- net +6, exactly this iteration's own 6 repos, zero regressions, zero repos gained or lost outside the targeted set.", :event/not-done "Did not register any new west-orphans this iteration -- all 6 targets were already west-registered (verified before dispatch), so no repos.edn/manifest-orphan-registration work was needed or done. Did not attempt a 7th repo -- 6/6 clean was treated as a complete, honestly-verified batch per this rollout's standing guardrail against chasing a round number. Did not touch checklist items 1/3/5/7 for any of the 6 newly-closed repos, nor promote any of the now-91 item2+4+6-closed repos to the flagship cohort table (cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn) -- consistent with every prior new-vertical entry in this ledger. Did not resolve an open naming/framing discrepancy flagged by the isic-6810 agent: the repo's own blueprint.edn/README self-describe it as 'Community Real-Estate Agency' with a closing/title-transfer workflow (closer to brokerage framing), even though its ISIC code (6810, own-or-leased-property) and this iteration's intent was a rental-operator framing distinct from isic-6820's already-closed fee-basis agency business; the underlying governor/store code and HARD-hold rule set ARE genuinely different from isic-6820's (no-spec-basis/sanctions-hit/incomplete-documents vs. isic-6820's own rule set), so the item2/4/6 closure itself is real and correct, but the sector-diversity claim for this specific repo should be read with that caveat rather than as a clean new 'rental operations' example -- flagged honestly, not resolved. Did not fix the pre-existing `cloud-itonami-isic-8291` `dossier/llm.cljc:254` forward-reference compile bug, independently re-encountered by BOTH the isic-6420 agent this iteration AND (per seq22's own ledger entry) the isic-6622 agent last iteration -- two independent hits on the same live upstream bug is a stronger signal it is real and worth a dedicated future iteration, still out of scope for this one. Did not fix isic-6810's own separately-broken `ci.yml` test job (checks out siblings at the wrong org path, `orgs/com-junkawasaki/langgraph-clj` instead of `orgs/kotoba-lang/langgraph`, failing since 2026-07-14 per the agent's own investigation of its live CI log) -- this iteration's own `regenerate.yml` uses the correct paths and is unaffected, but the repo's pre-existing test-job breakage itself was left unfixed as out of scope. Did not resolve the recurring OAuth workflow-scope friction (worked around per-repo via SSH remote again this iteration, as in prior iterations) -- still flagged as a cheap follow-up requiring an interactive device-flow consent this unattended session cannot complete.", :event/template-track-record "91 repos fleet-wide now have item2+4+6 ALL closed (measured via a direct full-EDN-parse intersection query, not just reading 3 separate aggregate counters), up from 85 at this iteration's own first fresh scan -- net +6, zero unattributed drift, zero regressions, zero drops of a dispatched repo (the 7th consecutive iteration since seq16 with a 100% attempted-to-landed ratio on this template; no repo has been dropped by this specific template-application pattern in any iteration from seq16 through seq23). This iteration's own 6 new-sector closures: cloud-itonami-isic-6810 (realty, real estate with own/leased property -- rental-operator framing, though see :event/not-done for an honest caveat about the repo's own internal agency-leaning framing text), cloud-itonami-isic-8121 (buildingcleaningops, general cleaning of buildings), cloud-itonami-isic-7710 (vehiclerentalops, renting/leasing of motor vehicles), cloud-itonami-isic-6420 (holdco, activities of holding companies), cloud-itonami-isic-5224 (cargohandling, cargo handling), cloud-itonami-isic-7721 (recreationalrentalops, renting/leasing of recreational and sports goods) -- adding to a fleet-wide sector list now spanning roughly 74 distinct real-world sectors (68 cited at seq21/22 plus these 6 genuinely new ones). isic-4322-class bug check: CLEAN on all 6, independently re-verified by direct source read (not just trusting agent self-report) -- continues the unbroken clean streak from every iteration since seq16 first found and fixed that bug class. This iteration also independently corroborated the isic-8291 dossier/llm.cljc:254 upstream compile bug (first surfaced at seq22 via isic-6622's test run) via a SECOND, unrelated agent (isic-6420) hitting the identical error at the identical line -- a stronger signal than a single occurrence that this is a real, live, recurring defect worth a dedicated future iteration rather than an isolated fluke. Task-brief candidate categories that turned out ALREA