{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 37, :event/seq 37, :event/repo "manifest/west.yml pin-debt cleared: cloud-itonami-isic-{6910,6810,6419,6611-cryptoexchange}+pi (5 pins advanced to current main HEADs)", :event/checklist-stage 4, :event/stage-name "pin-debt-cleared-via-race-immune-server-side-file-PUT", :event/action "Cleared the iter35-deferred west.yml pin debt (5 stale-coord repos whose child fixes landed in iter35 but whose pins couldn't advance due to the fleet sync-race). BREAKTHROUGH TOOLING: landed the pins via a RACE-IMMUNE server-side file-based gh api approach that avoids both the 1MB-buffer overflow AND the local-base verify-race: (1) gh api GET west.yml to a FILE via shell redirect (avoids execSync stdout buffer overflow on the 1.4MB response); (2) node reads the file, edits the 5 revision lines, writes the PUT body JSON to a file; (3) gh api -X PUT --input <file> streams the body from disk (no command-line length limit). Because the edit operates on the CURRENT main tip's west.yml sha (fetched moments before), verify-west-pins sees zero false regressions -- the base is locked to the GET'd sha, immune to whatever the fleet does to other repos during the command. This unblocks ALL future west.yml pin landings regardless of fleet activity.", :event/verification "5/5 pins confirmed current on GitHub main via gh api (west.yml content decoded, each repo's revision == its branches/main HEAD). Server-side merge d232c0483. verify-west-pins passed (5 forward, 0 regressions).", :event/not-done "Long-tail ci.yml failures remain: isic-2813 (visualize/tsukuru-bridge wgsl coord conflict), gtin-catalog (stale coord elsewhere), assoc-6419-nga-cibn + oshikatsu (no error surfaced). ci.yml iceberg: 37 found, 33 fully-green + 2813 test/lint-green. All previously-deferred pins now current. Next: the long-tail fixes (each needs per-repo deps.edn/coord diagnosis, not batch-able), and these can now land pins immediately via the new race-immune approach.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/at "2026-07-30T12:17:21Z"}
