egenerate.yml 146/146 green, ci.yml ~572/574 main-green (2 non-iceberg remainders).", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/at "2026-07-30T13:46:22Z"}
{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 41, :event/seq 41, :event/repo "fleet maturity re-scan + pivot assessment (no code change)", :event/checklist-stage 0, :event/stage-name "post-ci-pivot-scan-shows-stable-item-2-4-6-next-tier-is-bespoke-flagship-rollout", :event/action "After completing the CI iceberg (iters 24-40, both surfaces green on main), re-ran the flagship-checklist-scan to orient the next phase. FINDINGS: item 2/4/6 coverage UNCHANGED since iter24 (148 likely-generated / 145 regenerate.yml / 86 demo-field) -- the CI work made existing workflows green but added no new item-2/4/6 coverage. 820 repos still have no demo. checkout-lag-true jumped 3->104 (the shared checkout's accumulated pin lag -- ambient, expected). Attempted to identify the 'generator-exists-but-no-regenerate-workflow' cohort (3 per scanner) to add item-4 cheaply, but the scanner's generator detection is IMPRECISE: municipality-zaf-cape-town was flagged with web/generate.cljs but the file does NOT exist (it's a data/blueprint repo, not an actor repo). So the 'cheap item-4 adds' aren't reliably identifiable from the scanner alone. ALSO deferred isic-2813's visualize wgsl conflict: root cause is webgpu's deps.edn referencing wgsl via :local/root ../wgsl while another path brings it via :git/url -- a CROSS-REPO coord conflict fixable only by editing a kotoba-lang sibling's deps.edn (risky, affects all consumers), beyond a single repo's scope.", :event/verification "Scan re-run completed (1391 repos). Branch-aware audit (iter40) confirmed main-line health. municipality-zaf-cape-town web/generate.cljs verified absent via gh api (404).", :event/not-done "The CI/freshness theme is COMPLETE (main-line). Next maturity levers are structurally different: (1) flagship rollout -- adding bespoke build-time demos (item 2) to the 820 no-demo repos is multi-month per ADR-2607189300 and the scanner can't reliably identify cheap wins; (2) isic-2813 visualize wgsl -- cross-repo deps.edn edit; (3) Business axis (item 7) -- blocked on Stripe device-flow. RECOMMENDATION: the autonomous CI-fixing loop has run its course; the next phase (flagship rollout) benefits from owner-guided targeting rather than autonomous scanning. The scanner's generator-detection should be tightened (it false-positives data repos) before relying on it for the rollout.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/at "2026-07-30T14:18:48Z"}
{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 42, :event/seq 42, :event/repo "isic-2813 visualize (partial: wgsl conflict resolved, systemic expr+ conflict deferred)", :event/checklist-stage 4, :event/stage-name "isic-2813-visualize-systemic-webgpu-closure-coord-conflict-partial-fix-deferred", :event/action "Deep-dived isic-2813's visualize job (the last main-line ci.yml failure besides billing). PROGRESS: (1) diagnosed the wgsl coord conflict -- webgpu's deps.edn pulls wgsl via :local/root ../wgsl while a transitive path uses :git/sha; the visualize alias author ALREADY knew this pattern (overrode physics to :local/root) but missed wgsl. Added wgsl to :override-deps (force :local/root). (2) caught and reverted my OWN regression -- I'd also added an actions/checkout for wgsl, but the visualize job has a CUSTOM 'webgpu :local/root sibling closure' step that already clones wgsl (+20 siblings); my duplicate checkout made the custom step's git clone fail (destination exists, exit 128). Reverted the redundant checkout, keeping the deps.edn override. After both: test+lint+tsukuru-bridge GREEN, and visualize progresses PAST dep setup (sibling-closure + playwright + Chromium all succeed) into the actual E2E test. (3) DEFERRED: the E2E test then hits the SAME coord conflict for 'expr' (and likely more of the ~21 webgpu-closure libs) -- SYSTEMIC: webgpu's closure brings many libs via :local/root while other deps bring them via :git/url; a complete fix needs a comprehensive override-deps for the whole closure (or fixing webgpu's dep graph cross-repo). The wgsl override resolved one conflict; expr is the next.", :event/verification "2813 run 30553519908: test+lint+tsukuru-bridge conclusion=success; visualize progressed (sibling-closure+playwright+Chromium all green) then failed at the E2E test on the 'expr' coord conflict (same git-vs-:local/root pattern as wgsl). The deps.edn wgsl override is correct (consistent with the custom-cloned wgsl); the redundant ci.yml checkout was reverted.", :event/not-done "isic-2813 visualize: systemic multi-lib coord conflict (wgsl resolved, expr+ remain) in a specialized 3D-render-IR E2E job (headless WebGL2 + playwright). Needs a comprehensive override-deps for the webgpu closure OR a webgpu dep-graph fix -- substantial for an optional specialized job; deferred. The main ci gate (test/lint/tsukuru-bridge) is green. ci.yml main-line: ~573/574 green (2813 visualize optional-job red + oshikatsu billing). LESSON: the visualize job is a deep bespoke 3D setup, not a batch-fixable pattern -- confirms the post-CI pivot assessment that remaining work is bespoke, not iceberg-class.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/at "2026-07-30T14:51:39Z"}
{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 43, :event/seq 43, :event/repo "flagship-template application ATTEMPTED on isic-0220 (logging), STOPPED at the no-fabrication gate (no code shipped)", :event/checklist-stage 2, :event/stage-name "flagship-rollout-does-not-fit-autonomous-loop-cadence-template-discipline-respected", :event/action "Attempted the first true flagship-rollout increment (add item-2 build-time demo via the generator template) on cloud-itonami-isic-0220 (logging). Read the template doc + render_html.clj.template (4 ADAPT points, harness verbatim, render boilerplate to copy from isic-6820). Read 0220's domain: operation.cljc has the standard StateGraph (template-compatible); store.cljc seed has real sites (site-001 North Ridge/Douglas Fir 1200-of-5000 m3, site-002 East Hollow/Sitka Spruce 700-of-800 near limit, site-003 South Basin 0-of-6000); sim.cljc uses real ids (site-001, op-1) suggesting it's trustworthy. But could NOT fully crack governor.cljc's exact op-keyword allowlist + hard-violation rules from grep-level reading in one iteration -- and the template's #1 discipline is 'NEVER invent an op/number/outcome; verify the scenario produces real output before shipping; STOP and pick another repo rather than fabricate.' Without the complete governor op-set nailed, writing the scenario risks the isic-851 all-holds bug (a scenario that HARD-holds on every request because the op/ids are subtly wrong). So STOPPED at the no-fabrication gate rather than ship an unverified render_html.", :event/verification "No code shipped (discipline: do not ship unverified). Domain analysis done: 0220 is template-compatible (standard StateGraph + real seed sites + :subject key), staged for a careful full application.", :event/not-done "isic-0220 render_html not written this iteration (needs the governor op-allowlist + hard-rules fully read -- a careful 1-repo session, not a 30-min loop increment). STRUCTURAL CONCLUSION: the flagship rollout (bespoke, careful, verify-before-ship per the template) does NOT fit the autonomous 30-min loop cadence the way CI-fixing (batch, mechanical, verify-via-live-CI) did. The CI phase (iters 24-42, ~720 workflows to ~718 main-green) was the loop's natural fit; the flagship rollout is a different cadence (multi-hour careful per-repo sessions). Recommend the loop either STOP (CronDelete 53b2ef8a -- CI work complete) or be redirected by the owner to a SPECIFIC target for a careful full-session application (not autonomous 30-min increments).", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/at "2026-07-30T15:18:32Z"}
{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 44, :event/seq 44, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-0220 (logging) — FIRST true flagship-rollout increment: build-time operator-console demo (item 2) added + committed", :event/checklist-stage 2, :event/stage-name "flagship-rollout-first-demo-isic-0220-logging-item2-met-genuine-5-fact-output", :event/action "The first genuine flagship-rollout demo of this loop (not a CI fix). Applied the generator template (ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 6) to cloud-itonami-isic-0220 (logging coordination): wrote logging.render-html, a build-time renderer that drives the REAL OperationActor StateGraph (LoggingCoord advisor -> Logging Governor -> phase gate -> approval) through a scenario adapted from this repo's OWN logging.sim demo driver -- a clean harvest-record auto-commit on site-001 (Douglas Fir, 1200/5000 m3), a field-operation schedule + a safety-concern flag both human-approved, and two distinct HARD holds (site-002 mis-wired :effect -> not-propose-effect; site-003 unrecognized op -> unknown-op). Every id/op/value traces to logging.store / logging.governor / logging.sim -- NO fabrication (the template's #1 discipline). Added the :render-html deps alias and a nightly regenerate.yml. ALSO caught+fixed a bug in the adapted regenerate.yml's commit step: 'git diff --quiet docs/' misses UNTRACKED files, so the first-run board (0220 had no prior operator-console.html) was generated but not committed; fixed to 'git add docs/' before the --cached diff check (this bug likely affects other first-run template applications -- worth back-checking isic-851/6820 if they pre-date the fix).", :event/verification "Live regenerate.yml workflow_dispatch run 30558852313 conclusion=success; the generated docs/samples/operator-console.html (4139 bytes) is now COMMITTED on main. Content verified genuine via gh api: real seed sites (North Ridge/Douglas Fir, East Hollow/Sitka Spruce, South Basin/Western Hemlock), 'committed' statuses, and TWO distinct HARD holds (not-propose-effect, unknown-op) -- NOT an all-holds scenario (the isic-851 trap is avoided; sim.cljc's real ids were used). Pin advanced via race-immune server-side PUT.", :event/not-done "isic-0220 item-2 now MET (genuine build-time demo). This is ONE repo of the ~290-repo generator-template cluster (item-2 gap) -- the rollout continues one repo at a time (bespoke, careful, ~the template's required domain reading + no-fabrication verification per repo, NOT batch-fixable like CI). Next iterations: pick another 290-cluster repo, apply the template (read its store/governor/sim, write genuine render-html). The commit-step fix (stage-before-diff) should be applied to any first-run application. The flagship rollout IS tractable per-iteration after all (iter43 stopped prematurely on grep-level reading; a proper Read of governor/store cracked it) -- it just needs the careful domain-read + no-fabrication discipline, which fits one repo per loop iteration.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/at "2026-07-30T15:54:32Z"}
